- Suite persistence: typed a 45-char draft in .topField, scrolled .index to 260,
  switched Notes -> Tasks -> Timeline -> Notes. Draft identical, index scrollTop
  still 260. The suite's central claim holds.
- Rover reach in tasks.dense: exhaustive up/down/right traversal reaches all 32
  visible cards. No unreachable card.
- Roving tabindex is consistent across all four surveyed states (one stop per
  group, -1 on the rest); the rail's arrow walk reaches the account tile at
  position 6.
- notes.voice focus trap: 28 tabs cycle exactly two controls.
- Space on .tick (role=checkbox) ticks; it does NOT pick the card up
  (src/tasks.js l.2916 guards it). Contract key intact.
- .idxRow hover is alive (my first sweep hit row 0, which is [data-cursor] and
  already carries --wash — false positive, withdrawn).

### FINDING 2 — every Tasks lane becomes a 13–44px sideways scroller between
### 1199 and ~1420, and one trackpad gesture slides the cards out of register.
Mechanism: src/tasks.css l.1053-1078. `.cardDots` grows a 24px mark into a 44px
target with `padding: 10px` + `margin: -13px -10px -13px auto` and
`box-sizing: content-box`. The negative right margin pulls the box back
VISUALLY, but negative margins do not shrink an ancestor's scrollable overflow,
and `.trayBody` is `overflow-x: auto`. Measured (tasks.dense, fresh page, no
interaction):
  .trayBody scrollWidth-clientWidth  @1440 [0,0,0,0,0]
                                     @1400 [3,4,0,0,0]
                                     @1360 [11,12,2,0,0]
                                     @1320 [19,20,10,0,0]
                                     @1280 [27,28,18,0,0]   <- declared viewport
                                     @1200 [43,44,34,0,0]   <- board floor is 1199
  tasks.board @1280 [13,14,4,0,0]; tasks.compact @1200 [11,12,0,0,0].
The offending descendant is .cardDots, right edge 23px past .trayBody's right
edge; the cards themselves sit 6px INSIDE it.
Reachable: one `mouse.wheel(80, 0)` over the To do lane at 1280 sets
scrollLeft 27/27. Screenshot _zz-ev-wheelshift.png: the whole To do column has
slid left, the first card's tick circle is sliced in half by the lane's left
edge, the ··· menu is exposed, and the column is now visibly out of register
with its own "TO DO 10" heading, which did not move.
No fade, no snap, nothing in the scrolled region — the guillotine edge from the
lessons file, at a width the console screenshots.

### FINDING 3 — the head's completion meter is the one number on a filtered
### sheet that never says what it still describes.
tasks.board @1440. Press .who "Mara & Finn", then the "1 overdue" chip. Board
shows 0 cards. Every lane restates itself honestly ("To do, 0 of 3 shown",
visible "0/3"); the empty state says "Nothing matches. No overdue task is on the
board for Mara & Finn. All 13 are hidden." and offers "Show all work".
The head still reads "5 of 13 done  ▬▬▬▬  38%" with the pace bar filled, and
[role=meter] still carries aria-valuenow=5 / aria-label "5 of 13 done, 38
percent", unqualified. Screenshot _zz-ev-filterhead.png. Same in the List view.
The lessons file's own rule: "Header counts must say what they still describe
while a filter hides things."

### FINDING 4 — every board card is spoken about three times.
page.accessibility.snapshot() on .card[data-id="demo-t-01"], tasks.board @1440:
  article name  "Confirm marquee sides with the hire company"
  article desc  "Mara & Finn, Saturday. …by Thursday. Mara & Finn. High priority."
  > paragraph   "Confirm marquee sides with the hire company"      (title, 2nd)
  > generic     "Mara & Finn, Saturday. …by Thursday. Mara & Finn. High priority."
                                                                    (the sr span
                                                                     itself, 2nd)
  > paragraph   "Mara & Finn, Saturday. …by Thursday."             (note, 3rd)
  > button      "Mara & Finn"                                      (tag, 3rd)
  > text        "High" + "priority"                                (pri, 3rd)
src/tasks.js l.461 builds `<span class="sr" id="cd-…">` purely as the
aria-describedby target and leaves it in the reading order; `.sr` hides it from
sight, not from AT. 13 cards on the board, 32 in dense. Round 6 fixed exactly
this on the seam's card ("does not say it twice to a screen reader either") and
left it on every board card.

### FINDING 5 — a done card stops saying it is movable and stays movable.
src/tasks.js l.448: `(done ? "" : ' aria-roledescription="Movable task"')`.
l.449 emits aria-keyshortcuts="Space ArrowUp ArrowDown ArrowLeft ArrowRight"
unconditionally. Driven: all 5 cards in Done have rd=null, ks present; Space +
ArrowLeft on demo-t-09 moved it to Waiting and the roledescription reappeared.
So 5 of 13 cards advertise shortcuts with no word for what they do.

